---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import LessonIllustration from "../../components/LessonIllustration.astro";
import StructureFacts from "../../components/StructureFacts.astro";
import SetStructureDemo from "../../components/SetStructureDemo.astro";
import TermCallout from "../../components/TermCallout.astro";
import { twoPSetTerm } from "../../lib/atlas/standalone-terms";
import "../../styles/set-lesson.css";

const tombstoneTerm = {
  term: "tombstone",
  definition: "Retained removal metadata that prevents an old addition from becoming live again.",
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="TwoPSet"
  description="Alice retires the old Eagle Creek beacon, but its permanent removal record blocks Bob's replacement."
  territory="Structures"
  sheetTitle="TwoPSet"
>
  <article class="set-lesson">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="territory-label">Structures</p>
      <h1>TwoPSet</h1>
      <p class="structure-summary">
        A GSet can record every beacon the hikers find, but it cannot remove
        one. The hikers add a second GSet for permanent removals. Together,
        those two grow-only sets form a TwoPSet.
      </p>
      <LessonIllustration id="structures-two-p-set" />
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="notebook-setup-title">
      <h2 id="notebook-setup-title">Each hiker carries the same two-page notebook</h2>
      <p>
        Each page is a separate GSet. The additions page records every beacon
        name a hiker has received. The removals page records every name that a
        hiker knows is permanently retired. Both pages only grow, and the
        hikers merge each page by union.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before the ranger sends them out again, Alice's Eagle Creek report has
        reached all three hikers. Alice, Bob, and Carol each have{" "}
        <code>Eagle Creek</code> on the additions page and an empty removals
        page, so all three still show the beacon on their visible lists.
      </p>
    </section>

    <StructureFacts
      structure="TwoPSet"
      family="CRDT"
      model="State-based two-phase set"
      updates="Add, then remove permanently"
      merge="Union the addition set and the removal set."
      delivery="Removal survives repeated and out-of-order delivery"
      bestFor="Membership where retirement must be final"
      cost="Retain additions and permanent removal records"
    />

    <section aria-labelledby="retire-beacon-title">
      <h2 id="retire-beacon-title">Alice and Bob write on different pages</h2>
      <p>
        Alice finds that the old Eagle Creek beacon is gone, so she writes
        <code>Eagle Creek</code> on her removals page. Bob has not received
        Alice's record. He finds a replacement with the same name and writes
        <code>Eagle Creek</code> on his additions page, where the name is
        already present. Carol makes no change.
      </p>
      <p>
        That retained removal record is a{" "}
        <dfn><a href="/glossary/#tombstone">tombstone</a></dfn>. It prevents a
        delayed or repeated addition record from making the retired beacon
        visible again.
      </p>
      <TermCallout {...tombstoneTerm} />
      <p>
        A <dfn><a href="/glossary/#twopset">TwoPSet</a></dfn> is composed of
        those two GSets. A value is visible only when it appears in additions
        and does not appear in removals.
      </p>
      <TermCallout {...twoPSetTerm} />
      <figure class="notebook">
        <table aria-label="TwoPSet notebook contents at three checkpoints">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Checkpoint</th>
              <th scope="col">Notebook</th>
              <th scope="col">Additions page</th>
              <th scope="col">Removals page</th>
              <th scope="col">Visible list</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <th scope="rowgroup" rowspan="3">Before retirement</th>
              <th scope="row">Alice</th>
              <td><code>{"{ Eagle Creek }"}</code></td>
              <td><code>{"{}"}</code></td>
              <td>Eagle Creek</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Bob</th>
              <td><code>{"{ Eagle Creek }"}</code></td>
              <td><code>{"{}"}</code></td>
              <td>Eagle Creek</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Carol</th>
              <td><code>{"{ Eagle Creek }"}</code></td>
              <td><code>{"{}"}</code></td>
              <td>Eagle Creek</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <th scope="rowgroup" rowspan="3">Records apart</th>
              <th scope="row">Alice</th>
              <td><code>{"{ Eagle Creek }"}</code></td>
              <td><code>{"{ Eagle Creek }"}</code></td>
              <td>empty</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Bob</th>
              <td><code>{"{ Eagle Creek }"}</code></td>
              <td><code>{"{}"}</code></td>
              <td>Eagle Creek</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Carol</th>
              <td><code>{"{ Eagle Creek }"}</code></td>
              <td><code>{"{}"}</code></td>
              <td>Eagle Creek</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <th scope="rowgroup" rowspan="3">After exchange</th>
              <th scope="row">Alice</th>
              <td><code>{"{ Eagle Creek }"}</code></td>
              <td><code>{"{ Eagle Creek }"}</code></td>
              <td>empty</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Bob</th>
              <td><code>{"{ Eagle Creek }"}</code></td>
              <td><code>{"{ Eagle Creek }"}</code></td>
              <td>empty</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Carol</th>
              <td><code>{"{ Eagle Creek }"}</code></td>
              <td><code>{"{ Eagle Creek }"}</code></td>
              <td>empty</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <figcaption>
          Each hiker computes the visible list from the two pages in that
          notebook. Bob's replacement does not create a new set member because
          the same name is already on the additions page.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p>
        When the hikers exchange records, each notebook takes the union of the
        additions pages and the union of the removals pages. Every notebook
        ends with Eagle Creek on both pages, so all three visible lists are
        empty. A delayed or repeated additions page cannot erase the retained
        removal.
      </p>
    </section>

    <SetStructureDemo
      kind="two-p-set"
      title="Race retirement against replacement"
      description="Alice retires Eagle Creek while Bob reports the same name again. The permanent tombstone must win at all three notebooks."
      rule="Union additions and removals; removal wins forever."
      raceLabel="Race Alice's retirement and Bob's report"
    />

    <section aria-labelledby="replacement-title">
      <h2 id="replacement-title">The replacement cannot return</h2>
      <p>
        The name means <strong>two-phase set</strong>. Each beacon name can
        move from never added, to present, to permanently removed. A TwoPSet
        cannot distinguish two installations that use the same name. The next
        set gives every addition its own identity, so Alice can remove the old
        beacon while Bob's replacement survives.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="notes-title">
      <h2 id="notes-title">Sources and implementation</h2>
      <p>
        Watershed's{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/tylerbutler/watershed/blob/4a8739323ee491f353fcaa8ccfb0488419c1cd43/src/watershed/two_p_set_kernel.gleam">TwoPSet kernel</a>
        {" "}stores additions and permanent removals as two grow-only sets.
      </p>
    </section>

    <nav class="structure-next" aria-label="Continue through set structures">
      <a href="/structures/g-set/">Back to GSet</a>
      <a href="/structures/sets/">Browse set family</a>
      <a href="/structures/observed-remove-set/">Continue to observed-remove set</a>
    </nav>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
